this is the brute force way of solving the problem its simple just use a counter and loop the grid and count numbers which are less than zero

class Solution {
    public int countNegatives(int[][] grid) {
        // Number of rows in the grid
        int n = grid.length;
        // Number of columns in the grid
        int m = grid[0].length;
        // Variable to store the count of negative numbers
        int count = 0;
        // Traverse each row of the grid
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            // Traverse each column of the current row
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                // Check if the current element is negative
                if (grid[i][j] < 0) {
                    // Increment the count if the element is negative
                    count++;
                }
            }
        }
        // Return the total count of negative numbers
        return count;
    }
}
Time Complexity :- O(N x M);
Space Complexity :- O(1);

Better Approach - using binary search with the above implementation

class Solution {
    public int countNegatives(int[][] grid) {
        // Total number of rows in the matrix
        int rows = grid.length;
        // Total number of columns in the matrix
        int cols = grid[0].length;
        // Variable to store the total count of negative numbers
        int count = 0;
        // Traverse each row one by one
        for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {
            // Binary search boundaries for the current row
            int left = 0, right = cols - 1;
            // Stores the index of the first negative number
            //Initialised to cols assuming no negative number exists
            int firstNeg = cols;
            // Binary search to find the first negative element in the row
            while (left <= right) {
                // Calculate mid index safely
                int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;
                // If the mid element is negative
                if (grid[i][mid] < 0) {
                    // Update first negative index
                    firstNeg = mid;
                    // Move search to the left side to find earlier negative
                    right = mid - 1;
                } 
                // If the mid element is non-negative
                else {
                    // Move search to the right side
                    left = mid + 1;
                }
            }
            // Number of negative elements in the current row
            count += cols - firstNeg;
        }
        // Return the total count of negative numbers
        return count;
    }
}
Time Complexity :- O(rows x log(cols)).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
